# scicomp-research-skills commit message template.
#
# Lines beginning with '#' are stripped from the final commit message.
#
# Conventional-commit prefix examples:
#   feat: <new feature>
#   fix:  <bug fix>
#   docs: <documentation change>
#   chore: <housekeeping; no code-behaviour change>
#   ci:   <CI workflow change>
#   refactor: <code reorg without behaviour change>
#
# After the subject line + blank line, write the body explaining WHY
# the change was made (the diff already shows WHAT). Reference issues
# / PRs / journal entries that motivated the change.
#
# The Co-Authored-By trailer below records substantive AI assistance
# in this repo's commits per the maintainer-policy override in
# CONTRIBUTING.md "Maintainer-policy override: AI co-authorship
# attribution". Delete the trailer for human-only commits.
#
# More on git trailers: https://git-scm.com/docs/git-interpret-trailers
# More on this repo's policy: see CONTRIBUTING.md.



Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
